"elasticsearch['uid'] = 896\n"
"elasticsearch['gid'] = 896\n"
"rabbitmq['uid'] = 895\n"
"rabbitmq['gid'] = 895\n"
"guacd['uid'] = 894\n"
"guacd['gid'] = 894"
msgstr ""
"appliance_url 'https://morpheus.localdomain'\\nelasticsearch['es_hosts'] = "
"{'192.168.104.01' => 9200, '192.168.104.02' => 9200, '192.168.104.03' => "
"9200}\\nelasticsearch['node_name'] = "
"'192.168.104.03'\\nelasticsearch['host'] = '0.0.0.0'\\nrabbitmq['host'] = "
"'0.0.0.0'\\nrabbitmq['nodename'] = 'rabbit@node03'\\nmysql['enable'] = "
"false\\nmysql['host'] = {'127.0.0.1' => 6446}\\nmysql['morpheus_db'] = "
"'morpheus'\\nmysql['morpheus_db_user'] = "
"'morpheus'\\nmysql['morpheus_password'] = "
"'morpheusDbUserPassword'\\nuser['uid'] = 899\\nuser['gid'] = 899\\n# at "
"the time of this writing, local_user is not valid as an option so the full "
"entry is needed\\nnode.default['morpheus_solo']['local_user']['uid'] = "
"898\\nnode.default['morpheus_solo']['local_user']['gid'] = "
"898\\nelasticsearch['uid'] = 896\\nelasticsearch['gid'] = "
"896\\nrabbitmq['uid'] = 895\\nrabbitmq['gid'] = 895\\nguacd['uid'] = "
"894\\nguacd['gid'] = 894"

#: ../../getting_started/installation/3_node_ha/3_node_ha_morpheus_rb.rst:96
msgid ""
"The configurations above for ```mysql['host']`` shows a list of hosts, if"
" the database has multiple endpoints.  Like other options in the "
"configuration, ``mysql['host']`` can be a single entry, if the database "
"has a single endpoint:  ``mysql['host'] = 'myDbEndpoint.example.com`` or "
"``mysql['host'] = '10.100.10.111'``"
msgstr ""
"The configurations anterior for ```mysql['host']`` shows a list of hosts, "
"if the database has multiple endpoints. Like other options en la "
"configuration, ``mysql['host']`` puede ser a single entry, if the database "
"has a single endpoint:  ``mysql['host'] = 'myDbEndpoint.example.com`` o "
"``mysql['host'] = '10.100.10.111'``"

#: ../../getting_started/installation/3_node_ha/3_node_ha_morpheus_rb.rst:98
msgid ""
"The elasticsearch node names set in ``elasticsearch['node_name']`` must "
"match the host entries in elasticsearch['es_hosts']. ``node_name`` is "
"used for ``node.name`` and ``es_hosts`` is used for "
"``cluster.initial_master_nodes`` in the generated elasticsearch.yml "
"config. Node names that do not match entries in "
"cluster.initial_master_nodes will cause clustering issues."
msgstr ""
"The elasticsearch node names set in ``elasticsearch['node_name']`` must "
"match the host entries in elasticsearch['es_hosts']. ``node_name`` is used "
"for ``node.name`` y ``es_hosts`` is used for "
"``cluster.initial_master_nodes`` en la generated elasticsearch.yml config. "
"Node names that do not match entries in cluster.initial_master_nodes will "
"cause clustering issues."

#: ../../getting_started/installation/3_node_ha/3_node_ha_morpheus_rb.rst:100
msgid ""
"The rabbitmq['node_name'] in the Node 1 example above is "
"**rabbit@node01**.  The shortname for the server of node01 must be "
"resolvable by DNS or /etc/hosts of all other hosts, same for node02 and "
"node03.  FQDNs cannot be used here"
msgstr ""
"The rabbitmq['node_name'] in the Node 1 example above is "
"**rabbit@node01**.  The shortname for el servidor of node01 debe ser "
"resolvable by DNS o /etc/hosts of all other hosts, same for node02 y "
"node03.  FQDNs cannot be used here"

